#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:113
msgid "Memory Safety with BufferChangedEvent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:115
msgid "The Problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:117
msgid ""
"When a NumPy array references VTK buffer memory and the VTK array "
"reallocates (e.g., due to `Resize()` or `InsertNextTuple()`), the NumPy "
"array may point to invalid memory, causing crashes or data corruption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:121
msgid "The Solution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:123
msgid ""
"VTK data arrays now fire a `BufferChangedEvent` whenever they reallocate "
"their internal buffers. Python wrapper classes like `VTKArray` observe this "
"event and mark themselves as stale, raising a `RuntimeError` if accessed "
"after the buffer has changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:128
msgid ""
"When using `vtkBuffer` directly, you should obtain fresh buffer references "
"after any operation that might reallocate the array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:131
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:133
msgid ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"from vtkmodules.vtkCommonCore import vtkFloatArray\n"
"import vtkmodules.numpy_interface.dataset_adapter as dsa\n"
"\n"
"arr = vtkFloatArray()\n"
"arr.SetNumberOfValues(10)\n"
"arr.SetValue(0, 42.0)\n"
"\n"
"# Create a VTKArray wrapper (recommended for safety)\n"
"va = dsa.vtkDataArrayToVTKArray(arr)\n"
"print(va[0])  # 42.0\n"
"\n"
"# Resize the VTK array - this may reallocate the buffer\n"
"arr.SetNumberOfValues(1000)\n"
"\n"
"# VTKArray detects the stale buffer and raises RuntimeError\n"
"try:\n"
"    print(va[0])  # Raises RuntimeError\n"
"except RuntimeError:\n"
"    print(\"Buffer changed - get a fresh reference\")\n"
"\n"
"# Get a fresh VTKArray reference\n"
"va_new = dsa.vtkDataArrayToVTKArray(arr)\n"
"print(va_new.shape)  # (1000,)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:160
msgid "Improved numpy_support and dataset_adapter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:162
msgid "numpy_support Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:164
msgid ""
"The `numpy_to_vtk()` function now stores NumPy array references on the "
"buffer rather than the data array. This ensures the NumPy memory stays valid "
"even if the VTK array is modified:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:168
msgid ""
"from vtkmodules.util.numpy_support import numpy_to_vtk\n"
"import numpy as np\n"
"\n"
"data = np.array([1.0, 2.0, 3.0], dtype=np.float32)\n"
"vtk_arr = numpy_to_vtk(data)\n"
"\n"
"# The numpy array reference is stored on the buffer, keeping memory valid\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:178
msgid "dataset_adapter Module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:180
msgid ""
"The `VTKArray` class in the dataset adapter now stores a reference to the "
"underlying buffer, ensuring memory validity throughout the VTKArray's "
"lifetime:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:183
msgid ""
"import vtkmodules.numpy_interface.dataset_adapter as dsa\n"
"from vtkmodules.vtkFiltersSources import vtkSphereSource\n"
"\n"
"sphere = vtkSphereSource()\n"
"sphere.Update()\n"
"\n"
"# Wrap the output\n"
"wrapped = dsa.WrapDataObject(sphere.GetOutput())\n"
"\n"
"# Access point coordinates as VTKArray (numpy subclass)\n"
"points = wrapped.Points\n"
"\n"
"# The VTKArray holds a buffer reference, ensuring memory safety\n"
"print(points.shape)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:200
msgid "Best Practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:202
msgid ""
"**Use VTKArray for automatic safety**: The dataset adapter's `VTKArray` "
"class automatically detects buffer changes and raises `RuntimeError` on "
"stale access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:205
msgid ""
"**Get fresh references after modifications**: If you modify a VTK array's "
"size, obtain a new buffer reference and NumPy view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:208
msgid ""
"**Use zero-copy when possible**: Creating NumPy views via `np.asarray(buf)` "
"avoids data copying and provides the best performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkBuffer-in-python.md:211
msgid ""
"**Observe BufferChangedEvent for custom wrappers**: If you create custom "
"Python wrappers around VTK arrays, observe `BufferChangedEvent` to detect "
"reallocation."
msgstr ""
